{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":723105,"ns":0,"title":"Abstract simplicial complex","extract":"In combinatorics, an abstract simplicial complex (ASC), often called an abstract complex or just a complex, is a family of sets that is closed under taking subsets, i.e., every subset of a set in the family is also in the family. It is a purely combinatorial description of the geometric notion of a simplicial complex.","description":"Mathematical object","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}